# Theater (Operating Theatre) Patient Flow

## 0. Overview

This file is the direct Theater flow source of truth for the HOSSPI HMS implementation plan. Theater is a **surgical episode overlay on the IPD encounter** (or linked emergency/OPD context) — not a parallel admission system. It should stay aligned with the backend theatre-flow module (`GET /theatre-flows`, `POST /theatre-flows/start`, `update-stage`, checklists, anesthesia, post-op), the Flutter Theater workspace, and the upstream/downstream flows in [`.cursor/flows/ipd-flow.mdc`](./ipd-flow.mdc), [`.cursor/flows/opd-flow.mdc`](./opd-flow.mdc), [`.cursor/flows/icu-flow.mdc`](./icu-flow.mdc), [`.cursor/flows/nursing-flow.mdc`](./nursing-flow.mdc), [`.cursor/flows/emergency-flow.mdc`](./emergency-flow.mdc), and [`.cursor/app-write-up.mdc`](../app-write-up.mdc).

## 1. Goal

Enable surgeons, anesthetists, theater nurses, and theater coordinators to run surgical episodes end-to-end: schedule cases, complete safety checklists, record anesthesia, track intra-operative progress, capture post-operative notes, and **hand over back to ward, ICU, or outpatient care** — all anchored to the **same IPD admission / encounter** when inpatient.

Elective cases from OPD planning and emergency `THEATER` disposition must land in the theater workspace with source context preserved. Deliver a **professional theater workspace**: case board by stage, resource assignment (room, team), checklist-driven safety, and post-op handover summaries visible on ICU/Nursing detail.

### Central encounter rule

Every theater case, checklist, anesthesia record, and post-op note attaches to the **IPD admission / encounter** (or linked OPD/emergency source). Theater does not create duplicate admission records. OPD owns outpatient completion; IPD owns admission lifecycle; Theater owns the surgical episode overlay while the patient is in the OT pathway.

---

## 2. Position in the Patient Journey

Theater sits **on top of** the IPD encounter (or linked encounter from emergency/OPD) during the surgical episode.

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    OPD[OPD planned procedure] --> IPD[IPD admission for surgery]
    EMR[Emergency THEATER disposition] --> CASE[Theatre case started]
    IPD --> SCHED[Case scheduled]
    SCHED --> PRE[Pre-op checks]
    PRE --> OT[Transfer to OT — In Procedure]
    OT --> INTRA[Intra-op + anesthesia]
    INTRA --> POST[Post-op + PACU handoff]
    POST --> HO{Recovery destination}
    HO --> WARD[Ward — Nursing]
    HO --> ICU[ICU — icu-flow]
    HO --> OPD_OUT[OPD follow-up if day case]
    WARD --> IPD_CARE[IPD care loop continues]
    ICU --> ICU_CARE[ICU monitoring]
```

| Upstream | Flow reference | Theater responsibility |
| -------- | -------------- | ---------------------- |
| OPD elective surgery | [opd-flow §7](./opd-flow.mdc), `ADMITTED` | Preserve OPD encounter link; IPD owns admission |
| Emergency theater path | [emergency-flow §4](./emergency-flow.mdc) | Case from `THEATER` handoff with emergency context |
| IPD surgery order | [ipd-flow §7](./ipd-flow.mdc) | OT scheduling → pre-op → operation → post-op |
| IPD transfer | [ipd-flow §9](./ipd-flow.mdc) | Temporary OT/procedure transfer; return to ward/ICU |
| ICU post-op | [icu-flow §4.4](./icu-flow.mdc) | Post-op ICU handoff summary on ICU detail |
| Nursing post-op | [nursing-flow §4](./nursing-flow.mdc) | Post-op handover visible on nursing detail |
| Billing | [ipd-flow §4](./ipd-flow.mdc) | Pre-auth/deposit before high-cost procedure when required |

