## 3. Step-by-Step Theater Workflow

| Step | Stage | What Happens | Main Role |
| ---- | ----- | ------------ | --------- |
| 1 | Case indication | Surgery requested from IPD order, OPD plan, or emergency disposition. | Doctor / Emergency clinician |
| 2 | Case scheduling | `POST /theatre-flows/start` with admission/encounter link, procedure, surgeon, room, time. | Theater coordinator / Surgeon |
| 3 | Pre-op preparation | Pre-op checklist, consent verification, billing/pre-auth gate when policy requires. | Theater nurse / Anesthetist |
| 4 | Transfer to OT | IPD status `In Procedure / OT`; patient moved to theater ([ipd-flow §9](./ipd-flow.mdc)). | Ward nurse / Transport |
| 5 | Sign-in / Time-out | WHO-style safety checklists (`SIGN_IN`, `TIME_OUT`). | Surgeon / Anesthetist / Nurse |
| 6 | Intra-operative | `INTRA_OP` stage; anesthesia record, observations, procedure progress. | Surgeon / Anesthetist / Scrub nurse |
| 7 | Sign-out | `SIGN_OUT` checklist; operative note captured. | Surgeon / Team |
| 8 | Post-op / PACU | `POST_OP`, `PACU_HANDOFF`; recovery monitoring, post-op orders. | Anesthetist / PACU nurse |
| 9 | Handover destination | Return to ward, escalate to ICU, or day-case OPD follow-up per clinical decision. | Doctor / Theater nurse |
| 10 | Case closure | Stage `COMPLETED`; charges posted; IPD care loop resumes. | Theater coordinator / System |

---

## 4. Theater Entry Paths

### 4.1 Elective OPD → IPD → Theater

1. OPD doctor plans procedure and dispositions to `ADMITTED` ([opd-flow §3, §7](./opd-flow.mdc)).
2. IPD admission created for surgery ([ipd-flow §2.3](./ipd-flow.mdc)).
3. Pre-auth/deposit completed per policy.
4. Theater case scheduled with OPD source context on detail.

### 4.2 Emergency → Theater

1. Emergency clinician sets `THEATER` disposition ([emergency-flow §4](./emergency-flow.mdc)).
2. `startEmergencyTheatreFlow` creates theatre encounter and flow.
3. Case appears on theater board with emergency case context.
4. Billing may be deferred per [ipd-flow §4](./ipd-flow.mdc).

### 4.3 Inpatient ward → OT (temporary transfer)

1. Doctor places surgery order on IPD encounter ([ipd-flow §7](./ipd-flow.mdc)).
2. Theater case scheduled; IPD transfer to OT when patient leaves ward.
3. During case: IPD status `In Procedure / OT`.
4. Post-op: transfer complete back to ward or ICU with handover note.

### 4.4 Post-op → ICU

1. Clinical decision for critical recovery.
2. Theater completes `PACU_HANDOFF` and case closure steps.
3. Patient transferred to ICU bed; ICU module starts or continues stay ([icu-flow §4.4](./icu-flow.mdc)).
4. ICU detail shows theatre case summary when API provides reference.

