## 5. Backend Queue and Stage Contract

Frontend labels, filters, summary cards, badges, dialogs, and actions must use backend theatre-flow filters on `GET /theatre-flows` as canonical workflow states.

| Backend filter / field | User meaning | Primary owner |
| ---------------------- | ------------ | ------------- |
| `queue_scope=ACTIVE` | Scheduled or in-progress cases | Theater coordinator |
| `status=SCHEDULED` | Case booked, not yet in OT | Theater coordinator |
| `status=IN_PROGRESS` | Active surgical episode | Surgeon / Anesthetist / Nurse |
| `status=COMPLETED` | Case closed | Audit / Reporting |
| `status=CANCELLED` | Case cancelled with reason | Surgeon / Coordinator |
| `stage=PRE_OP` … `PACU_HANDOFF` | Workflow stage within active case | Theater team |
| `stage=COMPLETED` | All required checklists and records finalized | Coordinator |

### Workflow stage sequence (canonical)

`PRE_OP` → `SIGN_IN` → `TIME_OUT` → `INTRA_OP` → `SIGN_OUT` → `POST_OP` → `PACU_HANDOFF` → `COMPLETED`

Required checklist phases for closure: `SIGN_IN`, `TIME_OUT`, `SIGN_OUT`, `PACU_HANDOFF`.

Default landing scope: **Active cases** (`queue_scope=ACTIVE`).

