## 7. IPD and Transfer Integration

| Integration | Theater module behavior |
| ----------- | ----------------------- |
| IPD board `In Procedure / OT` | Sync when case is `IN_PROGRESS` and patient in OT |
| Request OT transfer | From IPD when patient in ward — [ipd-flow §9](./ipd-flow.mdc) |
| Complete return transfer | `update-transfer` with target ward/ICU bed; handover note |
| **Open in Theater** | IPD detail when active case exists |
| **Open in IPD** | Theater detail for admission-wide context |

---

## 8. Billing and Orders

Per [ipd-flow §4](./ipd-flow.mdc):

- High-cost procedures may require pre-auth or deposit before scheduling.
- Procedure charges post to IPD bill via billing integration.
- Post-op medication/lab orders use shared `clinical_actions` dialogs with `ClinicalRequestBillingPanel`.
- Theater does not run cashier workflows.

---

## 9. Cross-Flow Integration Rules

### IPD ([ipd-flow.mdc](./ipd-flow.mdc))

- §7 Surgery route: canonical order → theater execution path.
- §9 OT/procedure transfer: temporary movement; return with handover.
- §11 `In Procedure / OT`: case board and IPD status alignment.
- §16 encounter hub: case, anesthesia, checklists, post-op on admission.

### OPD ([opd-flow.mdc](./opd-flow.mdc))

- §3 `ADMITTED`: elective surgery admission handoff to IPD/theater.
- §5: theater team actions in theater workspace only.

### ICU ([icu-flow.mdc](./icu-flow.mdc))

- §4.4 Post-op → ICU: handover summary on ICU detail.
- ICU owns stay lifecycle after handoff — theater does not start/end ICU stays.

### Nursing ([nursing-flow.mdc](./nursing-flow.mdc))

- Post-op ward recovery: handover summary on nursing detail.
- MAR and ward vitals remain in Nursing module.

### Emergency ([emergency-flow.mdc](./emergency-flow.mdc))

- `THEATER` disposition creates case with `emergency_case_id` when available.

### Deep links

`/theater?id={caseDisplayId}&panel={checklist|anesthesia|postop|resources}` — router pre-selects case and focuses panel.

