## 10. Module Boundaries

From [app-write-up.mdc](../app-write-up.mdc):

| Own in Theater | Do not duplicate — use other module |
| -------------- | ----------------------------------- |
| Case scheduling, stage flow, checklists, anesthesia, post-op notes | IPD admission creation (except via upstream handoff) |
| Resource assignment (room, team) | Hospital-wide bed CRUD (Facility / IPD) |
| Operative documentation canonical record | Duplicate anesthesia in Clinical if theater owns record |
| Post-op handover summary | ICU stay lifecycle (ICU module) |
| Procedure charges trigger | Invoice/payment/cashier (Billing) |

---

## 11. Important Implementation Rule

The **IPD encounter remains the central record** ([ipd-flow §16](./ipd-flow.mdc)). Theater overlay data attaches to it:

- Theater case start, stage history, checklists
- Anesthesia and intra-op observations
- Post-op notes and PACU handoff
- Resource assignments
- Source OPD/emergency context (read-only links)
- Post-op orders (via IPD encounter)

Prefer `theatre-flow` actions as canonical over standalone theatre CRUD for workspace mutations unless admin/reporting requires direct CRUD.

